# PDF Builder — managing clients and API keys with the admin key.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above any block.
# Rider and Visual Studio open .http files natively.
#
# Set @host to 8080 when running under Docker. @adminKey is the key printed by
#   dotnet run --project tools/Blocks.Cli -- admin-key
# whose hash the service has in Blocks:Admin:KeyHash. The value below is the published, local-only
# key that compose.yaml is configured with: it works against `docker compose up` and nowhere else.

@host = http://localhost:5052
@adminKey = adm_lPQ25ykvuTW7HdOJLaJzfqnJsT4cKQfwwR5pgq4o


### Register a client — 201, Location: /api/admin/clients/ecommerce.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ecommerce", "name": "E-commerce" }


### List clients, ordered by id.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}


### Read one client.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}


### Issue a key that can submit and read jobs — 201. The response is the ONLY time the key is shown:
# copy "key" into the product's configuration now.
# @name issue
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce/keys
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "production", "scopes": ["pdf:generate"] }


### Use it: submit a job with the key just issued — 202.
POST {{host}}/api/pdf/jobs
X-Api-Key: {{issue.response.body.key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "invoice", "data": { "invoice": { "number": "INV-1" }, "items": [] } }


### Issue a key that only reads templates, expiring at the end of the year.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce/keys
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "template viewer", "scopes": ["pdf:templates:read"], "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z" }


### List the client's keys — name, permissions, dates, state and last use; never the key itself.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce/keys
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}


### Revoke the first key — 204, permanent. Within a minute every instance refuses it.
DELETE {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce/keys/{{issue.response.body.keyId}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}


### Disable the client — all its keys are refused with CLIENT_DISABLED within a minute.
PATCH {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "disabled": true }


### Enable it again — its keys that were not revoked work again.
PATCH {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "disabled": false }


### 409 CLIENT_ID_TAKEN — ids are permanent and never reused.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ecommerce", "name": "Again" }


### 400 VALIDATION_FAILED — ids are lowercase letters, digits and hyphens.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "E-Commerce", "name": "E-commerce" }


### 400 VALIDATION_FAILED — the message lists the permissions that exist.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients/ecommerce/keys
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "everything", "scopes": ["pdf:everything"] }


### 401 AUTH_REQUIRED — no key.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/clients


### 403 AUTH_SCOPE_MISSING — a client key, whatever its permissions, cannot manage clients.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Api-Key: {{issue.response.body.key}}
